  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>anova2</keyword>
  <short_description>Two-way analysis of variance.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>p = anova2(Y)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = anova2(Y, reps)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = anova2(Y, reps, displayopt)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[p, tbl, stats] = anova2(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>anova2</b> performs a balanced two-way analysis of variance. Rows represent levels of the row factor and columns represent levels of the column factor.</p>
    <p>When <b>reps</b> is greater than one, each row-factor level occupies <b>reps</b> consecutive rows. The returned p-values test columns, rows, and interaction. Without replication, interaction is not estimated.</p>
    <p><b>displayopt</b> can be <b>'on'</b> or <b>'off'</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[Y = [8 9 6; 7 8 5; 9 10 7; 12 14 11; 13 15 12; 11 13 10];
[p, tbl, stats] = anova2(Y, 2, 'off')]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
